<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the hardened runtime lets a signed Ordewell do (ADR-0060 H9). One file
  serves the app and, as entitlementsInherit, every binary inside it: the
  helpers (renderer, GPU, and the utility process the daemon runs in) and
  node-pty's spawn-helper. electron-builder.yml names it for both, so neither
  falls back to electron-builder's template, which grants more.

  An ad hoc build carries it too but runs without the hardened runtime, where
  these keys change nothing.

  Deliberately not granted:
  - allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8 maps its code pages with MAP_JIT,
    which allow-jit covers.
  - disable-library-validation: every native module (node-pty's pty.node, the
    daemon closure's addons) and spawn-helper are signed with this app's own
    identity, so library validation accepts them.
  - allow-dyld-environment-variables: nothing here loads code by DYLD_*.
  - App Sandbox, and with it the network and file entitlements: the app is
    distributed outside the Mac App Store, and the daemon must reach the
    repository, the runners and 127.0.0.1 as the person who started it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!--
      V8 compiles JavaScript to machine code at run time in the main process,
      every helper and the daemon's utility process. Without it the hardened
      runtime refuses the writable, executable pages and the app crashes at
      start.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
